---

### Layer Responsibilities

| Layer | Files | Responsibility | Must NOT |
|-------|-------|----------------|----------|
| **CLI** | `cli.rs` | Argument parsing, help, version | Business logic |
| **Commands** | `commands/*.rs` | Parse args → requests, prompts, output | Orchestration, crypto, I/O (partially deviated — see below) |
| **Application** | `application/*.rs` | Use case orchestration (`pack_bundle`, `run_bundle`) | Direct I/O, harness specifics |
| **Domain** | `domain/*.rs` | Types, validation, invariants | Any external dependency |
| **Harness** | `harness/*.rs` | Adapter implementations (`Harness` trait + registry) | Cross-harness logic |
| **Infrastructure** | `infrastructure/*.rs` | FS, archive, ignore, process | Domain logic |
| **Security** | `security/*.rs` | Crypto primitives | I/O, harness, domain logic |

---

### Status (v0.1.2)

**Fixed during v0.1.1/v0.1.2:**

1. ~~`application/run_bundle_impl.rs` imports `commands::run` types~~ — `application/run_bundle.rs` now owns `RunBundleRequest`/`RunResult`; `commands/run.rs` imports from the application layer (correct direction).
2. ~~`commands/pack.rs` calls `integrity`/`signing` directly~~ — the pack sequence (stage → encrypt secrets → checksum → manifest → canonical-JSON sign → validate) lives in `application/pack_bundle.rs`; `commands/pack.rs` delegates.
3. ~~Vestigial `application/init_bundle.rs`~~ — deleted (was uncompiled dead code referencing a nonexistent `Application` type).
4. ~~Bundle-root `launch` placeholder script~~ — no longer created by `pn init` (v0.1.2); launching is defined by `manifest.launch` only.

**Remaining deviations (tracked for v0.2):**

1. **`commands/init.rs`** does orchestration directly (Pi detection, directory scaffolding, manifest write) — there is no application-layer `init` use case yet.
2. **`commands/pack.rs`** still owns `--archive`/`--encrypt-archive` creation (tar.gz + passphrase prompt) after the application-layer pack succeeds.
3. **`commands/info.rs`, `commands/unlock.rs`, `commands/rekey.rs`** read manifests and touch crypto/domain directly instead of going through application-layer use cases.
4. **Harness Pi paths** — Pi-specific paths are acceptable inside the Pi adapter, but `commands/init.rs` and `commands/pack.rs` must not hardcode them once a second harness ships.

---

### Target Architecture (v0.2)

```
CLI → Commands → Application → Domain
                          ↓
              ┌───────────┼───────────┐
              ▼           ▼           ▼
           Harness   Infrastructure  Security
```

All dependencies flow **downward** (CLI → Commands → Application → Domain/Infra/Sec/Harness).
No upward or circular dependencies. v0.2 adds application-layer `init`/`info`/`unlock`/
`rekey` use cases so commands become pure adapters, and wires Aider end-to-end on
the existing `Harness` trait.
